    "Description": "The podman tool manages pods, container images, and containers. It is part of the libpod library, which is for applications that use container pods. Container pods is a concept in Kubernetes.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* golang.org/x/crypto/ssh: golang.org/x/crypto/ssh: Denial of Service via crafted AES-GCM packet decoder inputs (CVE-2026-46597)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* When using `--mount` in `podman run` results can be inconsistent, especially on /var/tmp (JIRA:RHEL-154348)\n\n*  [RFE] SELinux confined users unable to start podman.socket systemd user service (JIRA:RHEL-132875)\n\n* [RFE] Mounting of NFS Quadlet volume fails with permission denied (JIRA:RHEL-145863)\n\n* [RFE] podman API socket to support TLS/mTLS (JIRA:RHEL-91221)\n\n* Rebase podman to the latest upstream release [rhel-9.9] (JIRA:RHEL-168737)\n\n* podman does not clean up all files and leaves orphaned files consuming disk space [rhel-9.9] (JIRA:RHEL-173976)\n\n* [FJ9.8 Bug]: [REG]The \"podman-remote save\" command fails for rootless users. (JIRA:RHEL-186006)\n\n* podman: rebase to 5.8.5 (JIRA:RHEL-212537)\n\n* [FJ9.9 Bug]: [REG]The \"podman rm\" command can accidentally delete containers even though it is mounted by Buildah when used by a rootless user in remote. (JIRA:RHEL-211092)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nAdditional Changes:\n\nFor detailed information on changes in this release, see the Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9 Release Notes linked from the References section.",
